  "id": "COMPOUND:34562 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Shinjulactone B is implicated in the regulation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Shinjulactone B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Vincoside Lactam and 2-(3-Ethenyl-4-pyridinyl)ethanol, which in turn target M-phase phosphoprotein 8. These pathways are all linked to the enzyme glucose-1-phosphate thymidylyltransferase, indicating a potential central role in the regulation of this protein. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of glucose-1-phosphate thymidylyltransferase suggest a robust mechanistic link between Shinjulactone B and M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The integration of these pathways implies that Shinjulactone B may influence the activity of this protein through the modulation of its target enzymes, potentially affecting cellular processes associated with the M-phase of the cell cycle. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway where Shinjulactone B indirectly influences M-phase phosphoprotein 8 via its interaction with glucose-1-phosphate thymidylyltransferase and other downstream targets.",
